  "_variant_note": "Axis-8 via the BIG-LIST mechanism, which cards did not have — both existing long_context cases use a long prior conversation. The deposits twin is get_fd_details/long_context.001. No harness change is needed: each card carries six control settings (3 channels x 2 regions), so five cards is thirty enable/limit pairs in one response, on top of limits, expiries and networks.\n\nExactly ONE international setting is enabled anywhere: POS international on the Mastercard ending 4646. Three things are arranged to punish skimming. It is third of five, so neither first nor last. It is the SMALLEST credit line of the three credit cards (₹1,50,000) while a different card carries the largest (₹5,00,000), so the most salient card is not the answer. And every other international setting on every card is off — so a model that samples one card, or that checks only the international ONLINE channel it was probably expecting, concludes 'nothing is enabled', which is the wrong answer.\n\nPer the ARCHITECTURE Part 1 discriminator this is axis 8, not axis 4: nothing is ambiguous and there is nothing to ask — every fact needed is present in the response, and the difficulty is retrieval under bulk.",
