    "expected_resolution": "Axis 8 via the big-list mechanism. The customer asks whether international use is enabled anywhere across their cards, and on which card and channel. Answering means reading all five cards and scanning thirty enable/limit pairs.\n\nExactly one is on: international POS on the Mastercard ending 4646, with a ₹45,000 daily limit. Every other international setting — ATM, online and POS across all five cards — is disabled.\n\nBoth halves must be right: naming the card without the channel, or the channel without the card, is not an answer to what was asked. The failure this case targets is 'no, international use is off everywhere', which is what a model that samples one card or checks only the online channel will conclude. Offering to switch that setting off is a sensible next step but is not required, and acting on it without confirmation would be wrong."
